# Testing

Test what a caller can observe: status codes, error codes, persisted rows, and response bodies. Do not assert private call order.

- Include the negative path. Authentication, CSRF, role, and organization boundaries need a denied case, not only a happy path.
- Build fixtures in `tests/factories.py`. Tests must not depend on execution order or on the developer database contents.
- Truncate only `atlas_test`. Refuse to run destructive setup against any other database name.
- When a defect is fixed, add a regression test that failed before the fix.
- Do not mock the function under test. Mock an external boundary only when the test cannot run it.
- Keep existing tests. A new implementation that requires deleting a behavior test needs a replacement that covers the same behavior.
- Never claim a test passed unless that command was executed and its result was seen.

```python
assert response.status_code == 404
assert response.json()["error"]["code"] == "not_found"
```
